# Line endings are a correctness constraint here, not a style preference.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the default on Windows, including
# GitHub's windows-latest runners) checks every text file out as CRLF, while a
# developer machine ends up mostly LF because Prettier rewrites what it touches
# and its `endOfLine` default is `lf`. The result is that the same commit has
# different bytes on the dev box and on CI, per file, with no visible pattern.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it made `scripts/audit/atomic-write-audit.mjs` fail
# to import under Vitest on windows-latest only. The file starts with a shebang,
# and vite-node's shebang stripper does not account for the `\r`, so what was
# left did not parse — `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, 11 tests never
# collected, while the identical file passed everywhere else.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binary content and leave it untouched; every
# blob in this repo is already stored with LF, so this changes no history.
* text=auto eol=lf
